==English==

===Etymology===
{{abbreviation of|microphone|lang=en}} Attested since 1961.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmaɪk/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|aɪk|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{alt form|mike|lang=en||microphone}}
#* '''1987''', {{w|Eric B. & Rakim}}, ''[[w:I Know You Got Soul (Eric B. & Rakim song)|I Know You Got Soul]]''
#*: Picture a '''mic''', the stage is empty
#*: A beat like this might tempt me
#*: To pose, show my rings and my fat gold chain
#*: Grab the '''mic''' like I'm on Soul Train

===Verb===
{{en-verb|mics|micing|pres_ptc2=mic'ing|miced|past2=mic'ed}}

# {{alt form|mike|lang=en}}
#: ''If we add the drum kit, we'll have to '''mic''' the orchestra.''
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|title=Hunting Trophy Whitetails|page=167|author=Darren Brown|co-authors=Jackie Bushman|year=2002|passage=At 11:00 am, Doug '''mics''' up with me on the radio, and I advise him to go back to camp to get a quad, that we have a monster down.}}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|title=Gigs from Hell: True Tales of Rock and Roll Gone Wrong|page=104|author=Sleazegrinder|year=2003|passage=Imagine playing a venue the size of an aircraft hangar without your tiny amps '''miced''' up through the PA!}}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|title=The guerilla guide to the music business|page=164|author=Sarah Davis|co-authors=Dave Laing|year=2006|passage=This lacks the gut-punch of '''miced'''-up bass but hopefully the player can rise to the challenge and give his or her take extra energy to make up for it.}}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|title=Access all areas: a real world guide to gigging and touring|page=101|author=Trev Wilkins|year=2007|passage=Dynamics are used extensively for vocals, drums, and ''''micing''' up' amplifiers such as guitar amps but they can be used for almost any application.}}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|title=Sound and Recording|page=51|author=Francis Rumsey|co-authors=Tim McCormick|year=2009|passage=but it is extremely useful in applications such as vocals, drums, and the '''micing'''-up of guitar amplifiers.}}

